# LockSurface: entrance, exit, wake rules (Glass and Material; check in each look). Password "mock" (Rust only).
# Step 1: entrance. Default lockTransition is zoom; fade/none need a config change.
wait 1
rec enter-zoom 1.5 ipc lock lock
note FAILED earlier (Material): Rust showed black frames with the clock already in, then the circle within ~3 frames (50-100 ms); QML: black, then the circle with the clock inside opens over ~0.7 s. PASS: zoom - wallpaper scales 1.05 to 1 over ~450 ms while the content fades in and drops 20 px (Glass) / rises 32 px with the black circle opening (Material); the wallpaper is in the first frame the content starts moving (never black with the clock already in); start within ~800 ms of the surface map, ~450 ms of change.
# MANUAL: repeat with lock.lockTransition "fade" (only opacity) and "none" (everything there on the first frame): NOT RUN earlier
wait 1
# Step 2: exit
key mock
wait 0.3
rec exit 2 key -k Return
note PASS earlier in Material (lift ~220 ms). PASS: 220 ms out-cubic fade; zoom: content grows 8 % (Glass) / top lifts and bottom drops 5 % of height (Material), wallpaper leans in 5 %. Glass exit NOT measured.
wait 2
# Step 3: pointer wakes
ipc lock lock
wait 2.5
ptr move 960 300 sleep 300 glide 960 800 600
wait 1
shot pointer-glide
note A vertical-only pointer glide opens Material's pill (PASS earlier); Glass: no error and the lock still shows. Also check the Rust log for errors (MANUAL).
# NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness (move/glide did work earlier)
# Step 4: StandBy wake rules
ipc lock demo standby
wait 1.5
ptr move 900 500 sleep 300 glide 910 500 100
wait 1
shot glide-10
note A 10 px glide in StandBy leaves it in StandBy.
ptr move 900 500 sleep 300 glide 960 500 200
wait 1.2
shot glide-60
note A 60 px glide wakes the lock (morph back ~650 ms); lock visible.
ipc lock demo standby
wait 1.5
key -k Right
wait 0.8
shot standby-right
note The Right key changes StandBy's view (dots show) and stays in StandBy (PASS earlier).
key a
wait 1
shot key-wake
note A key wakes the lock, the field is focused; the waking key "a" must NOT be typed (no dot) - same as QML.
ipc lock demo standby
wait 1.5
ptr scroll 0 3
wait 1
shot scroll-next
note Scroll down moved to the next StandBy view (NOT RUN earlier; earlier the scroll command did not change QML either - check both).
# Step 5, 6: config
# MANUAL: lock.standbyWakeOnMouse false: a 200 px glide in StandBy stays
# MANUAL: with one screen set lock.standbyScreens ["NOPE"]: StandBy is black but a key still wakes
# Step 7: morph
ipc lock demo wake
wait 1.5
rec morph 1.5 ipc lock demo standby
note Morph: the big clock flies into StandBy's clock place (650 ms in-out), no pop at the end. (fade = 400 ms cross-fade, none = instant: MANUAL config variants)
wait 1
ipc lock demo off
ipc lock unlock
wait 2
